==Status Report: 2026-10-15 (media-card root cause + fix — missing Player commands)==

Root cause (confirmed against Media3 1.4.1 source)
--------------------------------------------------
Correction to the 2026-10-14 status, which rejected Gemini's "add
COMMAND_GET_CURRENT_MEDIA_ITEM / COMMAND_GET_TIMELINE" advice. That rejection was
half right, half wrong:

- Still correct: removing the synchronous `startForegroundNow()` bootstrap would
  reintroduce the first-play FGS deadline crash. Gemini's step 2 stays rejected.
- The error: we concluded the missing commands were irrelevant because
  `DefaultMediaNotificationProvider.createNotification` never calls those getters.
  That only inspected the *session* player (the raw `PlayerWrapper`). It missed that
  `MediaNotificationManager.shouldShowNotification()` never reads the session player
  at all — it reads the async *internal* `MediaController`, whose `PlayerInfo` is
  filtered by `PlayerInfo.filterByAvailableCommands(...)`:
      if (!canAccessTimeline && canAccessCurrentMediaItem && !timeline.isEmpty()) {…}
      else if (excludeTimeline || !canAccessTimeline) setTimeline(Timeline.EMPTY);
  where `canAccessTimeline` = COMMAND_GET_TIMELINE present and
  `canAccessCurrentMediaItem` = COMMAND_GET_CURRENT_MEDIA_ITEM present. TtsPlayer
  declared neither, so the controller's timeline was forced EMPTY,
  `shouldShowNotification` returned false, and the card was silently dropped before
  `createNotification` ever ran. This matches the device log exactly: only the plain
  bootstrap card shows.

So Gemini was right about the *missing commands* (the actual fix), though its stated
mechanism — "can't read the MediaItem, so can't get title/metadata" — was imprecise:
COMMAND_GET_METADATA was already present, and the real gate is the timeline filter
above (well articulated in today's trace: PlayerWrapper.createPlayerInfoForBundling
and MediaControllerImplBase apply the same WithCommandCheck filtering).

Fix
---
`TtsPlayer.kt` COMMANDS now adds `Player.COMMAND_GET_CURRENT_MEDIA_ITEM` and
`Player.COMMAND_GET_TIMELINE` (COMMAND_GET_METADATA was already present). The
synchronous `startForegroundNow()` bootstrap is kept as-is.

